#====================================================================
# E240 — macOS CoreGraphics display CLI capability split on OHOS
#====================================================================

id:                     E240
trigger_tool:           conan|cc|runtime
phase:                  porting|testing
error_signature:        ApplicationServices/ApplicationServices.h|CoreGraphics|CGDisplayCopyDisplayMode|CGConfigureDisplayWithDisplayMode|NativeDisplayManager

severity:               2
category:               platform-api-capability-split
match_keywords:         CoreGraphics, ApplicationServices, CGDisplay, NativeDisplayManager, display resolution, mode setter, unsupported boundary, screenresolution
title:                  Split macOS CoreGraphics display tools into OHOS-supported read-only capability and explicit unsupported boundaries

root_cause:             Some command-line display tools are built around Apple-only CoreGraphics display APIs. OHOS NativeDisplayManager public C APIs can query default-display width, height, and refresh rate, but they do not provide an equivalent physical display mode setter or a complete switchable mode enumeration in the API surface used by the port.
affected_scope:         Small macOS display utilities that combine current-mode query, mode listing, and physical display mode mutation in one CLI, such as screenresolution 1.6.
verification_cmd:       Run the OHOS package on a true device and require version/get to pass while list/set return non-zero with explicit unsupported diagnostics.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           capability-split-with-negative-tests
rec_description:        Keep the real OHOS capability implemented through NativeDisplayManager for read-only display metrics. Do not fake list/set success; implement unsupported diagnostics and assert those commands fail in test_package.
rec_command:            Add an OHOS backend using OH_NativeDisplayManager_GetDefaultDisplayWidth/Height/RefreshRate, return success only for -version/get, and add negative tests for list/set.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               source-patch-and-conan-test-package

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      mark-platform-invalid
fallback_description:   If no public target API can provide even read-only display metrics, reject the platform in validate() instead of shipping a misleading CLI.
fallback_command:       raise ConanInvalidConfiguration("no OHOS display backend available")
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          recipe-validate

forbid_1_pattern:       return\s+0;.*(list|set)|unsupported.*exit\s+0
forbid_1_reason:        Returning success for unimplemented mode listing or mode setting misrepresents the platform capability boundary.
forbid_1_consequence:   CI and downstream users can believe destructive display mode operations are supported when the OHOS backend only implements read-only metrics.

principles:
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             []
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

